---
const { expanded = true } = Astro.props;
---
<details open={expanded}><summary data-i18n="q1">What is an OopBuy spreadsheet?</summary><p data-i18n="a1">An OopBuy spreadsheet is a catalog for discovering and comparing products by category or keyword. This independent site uses a historical FindSpreadsheet export; open the OopBuy purchase page to check current details and place an order.</p></details>
<details open={expanded}><summary data-i18n="q3">Where can I see quality-check photos?</summary><p data-i18n="a3">After warehouse receipt, open OopBuy User Center → Warehouse to review available QC photos. Compare size labels, colour, stitching and visible damage. This preview does not have a live QC connection and its images may be incomplete.</p></details>
<details open={expanded}><summary data-i18n="q4">Is this the official OopBuy website?</summary><p data-i18n="a4">No. This is an independent product discovery site. OopBuy and the relevant sellers handle accounts, payments, warehousing, shipping and after-sales support.</p></details>
<details open={expanded}><summary data-i18n="q5">Are the displayed prices current?</summary><p data-i18n="a5">No. USD prices come from a historical catalog export and may differ from current prices, stock or options. Before paying, confirm the item price, seller-to-warehouse shipping and any other charges on OopBuy.</p></details>
<details open={expanded}><summary data-i18n="q7">How should I choose size and material?</summary><p data-i18n="a7">Review the seller’s size chart, material, colour and detail photos, then compare measurements with a garment that fits. Letter sizes vary by seller; contact OopBuy if an option is unclear.</p></details>
<details open={expanded}><summary data-i18n="q8">How is international shipping calculated?</summary><p data-i18n="a8">Destination, shipping route, packed dimensions and actual or volumetric weight affect the cost. Domestic shipping, international shipping, optional services and import taxes may be charged separately; check the current quote before submitting a parcel.</p></details>
<details open={expanded}><summary data-i18n="q9">Do QC photos guarantee product quality?</summary><p data-i18n="a9">No. QC photos help you inspect colour, labels, stitching and visible damage, but they do not guarantee authenticity, fit or durability. Contact OopBuy before international shipment if anything looks wrong.</p></details>
<details open={expanded}><summary data-i18n="q10">What if an item is damaged or I need a refund?</summary><p data-i18n="a10">Contact OopBuy promptly through the order with your order number, a description and photos, preferably before international shipment. Return eligibility, deadlines and fees depend on current seller and platform terms; a refund is not guaranteed.</p></details>
<details open={expanded}><summary data-i18n="extra_q1">How long can OopBuy hold items in the warehouse?</summary><p data-i18n="extra_a1">OopBuy’s beginner guide currently states that items receive 90 days of free storage after warehouse receipt. Check the start date, current deadline and any overdue charges in your account; policies can change.</p></details>
